{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-350830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =10\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4a}+\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}) \\\\  & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-4x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/ade58ce56684420fb0f00236af50bbb54f76801fc8870e1cce135cbd51f1b726.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }10{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a}) \\\\  & =10(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{4}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-350830" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350830" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5e^4}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3x+2}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3a+2}+\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-3x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/425e55256d2e53db1fce6684e2b7b05e8b487d5107dd4abacb8cf17add287c23.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-350845" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350845" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4x-3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4a-3}+\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-7}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-4x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/dd3903454e30d878fee3cd1f58f3942db034fde534e514f99e2c14ddd892a9b3.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-4a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{3}}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350847" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-350847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350847" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^{-7}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-3}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}]}_{a}^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-9}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{3x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/2f4fb9b35e0b68c6155ab9b945d10c36d08d878560e93d34d04e610d1983e50c.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-3}\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(\\frac{1}{3{e}^{9}}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6{e}^{9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-350810" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-350810" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5e^{-9}}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-1}^{a}{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x-1}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{e}^{-2x}]}_{-1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/0064a1c234adc9cf5d28d16696bef8a72384a8cc9f85ecc865c5d4ba36dc0d49.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2e}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{e}^{2a}}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e}(0-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2e}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{-{5}^{-x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{5}^{-x}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{a}}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/5949cbdface45cf103ae5bbd14db5d81917c19f3ef82417216e26d2064ca6bd1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{5}^{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-20501" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{3}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{2}^{x}]}_{a}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({2}^{3}-{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={2}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{2}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{2}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/b9a29cbd8a029e0f26e3da6a042ada0f8a809053233979bb4ff73db3dcf0f10d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{3}3\\cdot {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-351417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-351417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{5\\cdot {5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{5}^{x}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/2fc15149d2097a1965e575e725b4dfb49401c1fe5bb1c5b3e43bf0f4f51743a1.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-351417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-351417" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-351417" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{\\ln(5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{1}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{2}^{x}]}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({2}^{1}-{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (2-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={2}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{2}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{2}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/assets/b9a29cbd8a029e0f26e3da6a042ada0f8a809053233979bb4ff73db3dcf0f10d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}{2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (2-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{2}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/state.json" "file_sha256" "72467d1772803c4f69cd2ae61bea7112854ba56bd76303be3cadbb62f44fdaa4"} {"question" "q-152230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037234/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "abaa9270682b58d8b9e9a28aaa831c88fe855525b815e382ccfdc43dfe25035a"} {"question" "q-152230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha